alse" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,1256][1080,2337]" drawing-order="1" hint=""><node index="0" text="What's new since 2.5.2" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,1277][1028,1357]" drawing-order="1" hint="" /><node index="1" text="You're on the latest version (2.5.2). Here's what's in it:" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,1357][1028,1448]" drawing-order="2" hint="" /><node index="2" text="2.5.2  ·  14 November 2026" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,1448][1028,1564]" drawing-order="3" hint="" /><node index="3" text="• Day and night styles. Under Style, pick one style for the day and one for the night, and the app switches between them at sunrise and sunset, with the phone's dark mode, or with the light sensor. Sunrise and sunset are worked out on your phone; your location is never saved or sent. The switch fades over, and waits if you're touching the screen. Android Auto follows the car's own day and night with the same two styles.&#10;• Back up and restore. Under Diagnostics, save your settings, trip and code history, performance times and recorded drives to one file wherever you choose, and restore it on a new phone. Routes and your VIN are left out unless you tick them. Restoring shows what's in the file first, and only takes back what this app made: anything else in the file is refused.&#10;• Custom readings now refuse airbag module addresses, like the rest of the app." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,1564][1028,2264]" drawing-order="4" hint="" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>